<treenode node="validateAddress;PHP:Function Name;D:\www\imagecity\email\src\PHPMailer.php;f18;1182;5;1240;;;;vpos;;vbool;;r Definition     validateAddress($address, $patternselect = null)  Description      Check that a string looks like an email address. Validation patterns supported: * `auto` Pick best pattern automatically;s * `pcre8` Use the squiloople.com pattern, requires PCRE &gt; 8.0;s * `pcre` Use old PCRE implementation;s * `php` Use PHP built-in FILTER_VALIDATE_EMAIL;s * `html5` Use the pattern given by the HTML5 spec for &apos;email&apos; type form input elements. * `noregex` Don&apos;t use a regex: super fast, really dumb. Alternatively you may pass in a callable to inject your own validator, for example:  Parameters:     string $address - The email address to check     string|callable $patternselect - Which pattern to use;;d4,1183;;b1,5;;mstring $address;;pstring|callable $patternselect;;p">
</treenode>
